-- title:
--   Gaussian mixture likelihood-net errors and cardinality
-- statement:
--   For a probability measure \(G\) on \(K\subseteq\mathbb R^d\), define
--   \(f_G(x)=\int_K(2\pi)^{-d/2}e^{-\|x-\theta\|^2/2}\,dG(\theta)\).
--   For \(k=\binom{2L+d}{d}\), \(a=TS+S^2/2\), and
--   \[
--   h_L=\left[\frac{4e^{S^2}(S^2)^{2L+1}}{(2L+1)!}\right]^{1/2},
--   \qquad \rho_L=\frac{2e^{2a}a^{L+1}}{(L+1)!},
--   \]
--   define the global squared-Hellinger error and local log-density error by
--   \[
--   g=2h_L+\varepsilon^2+\frac{8k}{M},\qquad
--   \delta=(T+S)\varepsilon+\frac{4e^{2a}k}{M}+2\rho_L.
--   \]
--   The grid cardinality bound is \(N=(c^d)^{k+1}(M+1)^k\), where
--   \(c=1+\lfloor2S/(\varepsilon/(d+2))\rfloor_{\mathbb N}\).
--   Here the natural-number floor is truncated below at zero. The three error contributions correspond to moment approximation, location rounding, and weight rounding.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/hanshengjiang/reweighted-npmle-lean/blob/5af8d16822c5a8a3f032b13eb95daea40f307484/ReweightedNPMLE/GaussianNearMLE.lean#L20-L71

